  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1102 PM CDT Thu Jul 2 2026\n\nNo significant changes from the previous thinking in terms of the\nlong term forecast for our area. We are still expecting a \nsprawling ridge over most of the southern U. S. by Saturday. An \nupper level trough will move into the Great Lakes region Sunday \nnight into Monday, with the southern end of the trough slightly \nweakening the ridging over the Deep South. Medium range models \nhave backed off on the weak troughing for our area early next \nweek. This likely means lower chances for precipitation in our \narea, although we will still have low (20%-30%) chances for \nisolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms Monday into \nTuesday. Temperatures will change very little over the next \nseveral days with highs generally in the mid 90s to around 100 \ndegrees, and lows mainly in the 70s, although areas north of I-20 \nmay only get down to around 80 degrees at times.",
